main.py,backend/main.py,efbf882f3a66e4de8454857c767a96ab1a727c0c,straferxdranzex/docparser,https://api.github.com/repositories/971009157/contents/backend/main.py?ref=28370ac51483b0d4ff3fda1d08abb126c5921c9c,https://api.github.com/repositories/971009157/git/blobs/efbf882f3a66e4de8454857c767a96ab1a727c0c,https://github.com/straferxdranzex/docparser/blob/28370ac51483b0d4ff3fda1d08abb126c5921c9c/backend/main.py,,,0,0,0,1,2025-04-22T21:57:05Z,0,0,"# DocParser

An AI-powered document processing tool capable of analyzing Word (DOCX) and Excel (XLSX) files and extracting structured information based on user-defined criteria. The application supports Dutch, French, and English and is containerized for cloud deployment.

## Features

- Support for multiple file uploads (DOCX, XLSX)
- AI-powered information extraction using LangChain and OpenAI
- Multilingual support (Dutch, French, English)
- Web-based UI for defining extraction fields
- Export processed data in text or PDF format
- Docker-based deployment

## Prerequisites

- Docker and Docker Compose
- OpenAI API key
- Pinecone API key and environment

## Setup

1. Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone <repository-url>
cd docparser
```

2. Create environment files:

```bash
# Backend
cp backend/.env.example backend/.env

# Frontend
cp frontend/.env.example frontend/.env
```

3. Update the environment variables in both `.env` files:

- `OPENAI_API_KEY`: Your OpenAI API key
- `PINECONE_API_KEY`: Your Pinecone API key
- `PINECONE_ENVIRONMENT`: Your Pinecone environment

4. Build and start the containers:

```bash
docker-compose up --build
```

The application will be available at:

- Frontend: http://localhost:3000
- Backend API: http://localhost:8000

## Usage

1. Upload Documents:

   - Navigate to the web interface
   - Drag and drop or select DOCX/XLSX files
   - Click ""Upload""

2. Define Extraction Fields:

   - Select the language (English, Dutch, or French)
   - Add fields you want to extract
   - Click ""Start Extraction""

3. View and Download Results:
   - View the extracted information
   - Download results in text or PDF format

## Architecture

### Backend

- FastAPI for the REST API
- LangChain for document processing
- OpenAI for NLP tasks
- Pinecone for vector storage
- Docker containerization

### Frontend

- React with TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS for styling
- Axios for API communication
- Docker containerization

## Development

To run the application in development mode:

1. Backend:

```bash
cd backend
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate  # On Windows: venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
uvicorn main:app --reload
```

2. Frontend:

```bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm start
```

