suggestedQuestionsChain.py,backend/suggestedQuestionsChain.py,3fa7f9ec9941f61ebc49827ba194ffbdc7f7cf81,City-as-a-School-CAS/ARK,https://api.github.com/repositories/653362440/contents/backend/suggestedQuestionsChain.py?ref=7e0fd78b9dc395cde294af49ce5ce8723dd340b4,https://api.github.com/repositories/653362440/git/blobs/3fa7f9ec9941f61ebc49827ba194ffbdc7f7cf81,https://github.com/City-as-a-School-CAS/ARK/blob/7e0fd78b9dc395cde294af49ce5ce8723dd340b4/backend/suggestedQuestionsChain.py,,,0,2,269,518,2024-10-05T15:20:53Z,1,0,"# ARK: Your AI-Enhanced Learning Co-Pilot

ARK is an AI-enhanced learning co-pilot designed to facilitate self-guided learning in any domain. By utilizing the power of React and Langchain technologies, and APIs like OpenAI, ARK provides a comprehensive learning experience through various feature sets and resource-aggregating agents.

## Pre-requisites

Before proceeding with the setup, make sure you have the following software installed on your system:

- Node.js (version 14 or above)
- npm (version 6 or above)
- Python (version 3.8 or above)
- pip (version 19 or above)
- git
- gunicorn

Also, ensure that you have an active OpenAI API key. If you don't have one, follow the instructions [here](https://platform.openai.com/signup) to get the API key.

## Environment Setup

1. Create a `.env.local` file in the root of your project. This file will store your local environment variables, such as your OpenAI API key.

2. Reference the `.env.local.example` file in the repository to see which environment variables are required for ARK to run properly.

3. Fill in the environment variables in your `.env.local` file. For example:

    ```plaintext
    OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key
    ANOTHER_SECRET=some_secret_value
    ```

   Replace `your_openai_api_key` with your actual OpenAI API key and `some_secret_value` with the actual values needed.

4. If there are variables in the `.env.local.example` file that you do not know the values of, please contact a repository owner or a previous contributor to get the necessary values.

## Quick Start
If you prefer to quickly get started with ARK, follow the steps below:

1. Clone the repository:

    ```bash
    git clone https://github.com/City-as-a-School-CAS/ARK
    ```

2. Navigate to the cloned repository:

    ```bash
    cd ARK
    ```

3. Create a `.env.local` file in the root of your project and add your OpenAI API key:

    ```bash
    echo OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key > .env.local
    ```

   Replace `your_openai_api_key` with your actual OpenAI API key. This file is included in `.gitignore` to prevent accidental commit of sensitive information.

4. Install all necessary packages with:

    ```bash
    make install
    ```

5. Start the application with:

    ```bash
    make start
    ```

With these steps, ARK should be up and running on your local machine. Remember to replace `your_openai_api_key` with your actual OpenAI API key in step 3. If you encounter any issues, please open an issue on this repository.

## Installation

To install all necessary packages for ARK, you can use the `make install` command which will execute the following actions:

1. Install all necessary npm packages.
2. Install all necessary python packages.

## Starting the application

To start the application, use the `make start` command which will:

1. Start the frontend development server.
2. Start the backend development server with `uvicorn`, enabling live reloading.

## Formatting Code

To format the code, run:

```bash
make format
```
This will format Python code using black and sort imports using isort.

Deployment
To deploy the application, run:
```bash
make deploy
```

## Support
If you encounter any issues while setting up or running ARK, please send a message on discord or open an issue on this repository. Contributions, issues, and bug reports are welcome!"
