## Kubernetes Deployment

### Prerequisites

- Kubernetes cluster (v1.20+)
- kubectl configured
- Container registry access (Quay.io)

### Deployment Steps

#### 1. Create Namespace

```bash
# Create namespace
kubectl create namespace dn-academy-chatbot

# Set default namespace
kubectl config set-context --current --namespace=dn-academy-chatbot
```

#### 2. Deploy Database

```bash
# Deploy PostgreSQL
kubectl apply -f kube-vm/postgres.yaml

# Wait for database to be ready
kubectl wait --for=condition=ready pod -l app=postgres --timeout=300s

# Verify database deployment
kubectl get pods -l app=postgres
```

#### 3. Deploy Application

```bash
# Deploy chatbot application
kubectl apply -f kube-vm/chatbot_deployment.yaml

# Deploy service
kubectl apply -f kube-vm/service.yaml

# Deploy ingress
kubectl apply -f kube-vm/ingress.yaml

# Check deployment status
kubectl get deployments
kubectl get pods
kubectl get services
```

#### 4. Configure Ingress

```yaml
# kube-vm/ingress.yaml
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: Ingress
metadata:
  name: chatbot-ingress
  namespace: dn-academy-chatbot
  annotations:
    nginx.ingress.kubernetes.io/rewrite-target: /
    nginx.ingress.kubernetes.io/ssl-redirect: ""true""
    cert-manager.io/cluster-issuer: ""letsencrypt-prod""
spec:
  tls:
  - hosts:
    - chatbot.svc.dlytica.com
    secretName: chatbot-tls
  rules:
  - host: chatbot.svc.dlytica.com
    http:
      paths:
      - path: /
        pathType: Prefix
        backend:
          service:
            name: chatbot-service
            port:
              number: 8000
```

### Monitoring and Maintenance

#### Health Checks

```bash
# Check application health
kubectl exec -it deployment/chatbot -- curl localhost:8000/health

# View application logs
kubectl logs -f deployment/chatbot

# Check resource usage
kubectl top pods
kubectl top nodes
```

#### Scaling

```bash
# Scale application
kubectl scale deployment chatbot --replicas=3

# Horizontal Pod Autoscaler
kubectl autoscale deployment chatbot --cpu-percent=50 --min=2 --max=10

# Check scaling status
kubectl get hpa
```

#### Rolling Updates

```bash
# Update application image
kubectl set image deployment/chatbot chatbot=quay.io/datanature_dev/jupyternotebook:dlytica-chatbot-v51

# Check rollout status
kubectl rollout status deployment/chatbot

# Rollback if needed
kubectl rollout undo deployment/chatbot
```

### Configuration Management

#### Secrets

```bash
# Create secret for database credentials
kubectl create secret generic chatbot-db-secret \
  --from-literal=username=academy-chatbot-postgres \
  --from-literal=password=postgres_bot

# Create secret for OpenAI API key
kubectl create secret generic chatbot-openai-secret \
  --from-literal=api-key=your-openai-api-key
```

#### ConfigMaps

```bash
# Create configmap for application settings
kubectl create configmap chatbot-config \
  --from-literal=db-host=postgres-service \
  --from-literal=db-port=5432 \
  --from-literal=db-name=chatbot_db
```

