get_documents_by_natural_language.py,api/domain/graph_database/documents/get_documents_by_natural_language.py,6c007035b1ef684ae5adbe536c953bcbb57c00cb,mathimadsen17/faind-search-api,https://api.github.com/repositories/1050494223/contents/api/domain/graph_database/documents/get_documents_by_natural_language.py?ref=b7ff3be6b3819be41d5f525471cae2dede273852,https://api.github.com/repositories/1050494223/git/blobs/6c007035b1ef684ae5adbe536c953bcbb57c00cb,https://github.com/mathimadsen17/faind-search-api/blob/b7ff3be6b3819be41d5f525471cae2dede273852/api/domain/graph_database/documents/get_documents_by_natural_language.py,,,0,0,0,172,2025-08-29T16:23:19Z,0,0,"# Installation guide

The installation consist mainly of two steps

- Run the Docker container
- Expose the container with Nginx

## Run the Docker container

...

## Expose the container with Nginx

First, install Nginx and Certbot

```bash
sudo yum install nginx
sudo yum install certbot
sudo yum install certbot-nginx
```

Replace `nginx.conf` contents (using `sudo vim /etc/nginx/nginx.conf`) with:

```bash
# Global settings
user nginx;
worker_processes auto;
pid /var/run/nginx.pid;

events {
    worker_connections 1024;
}

http {
    include       /etc/nginx/mime.types;
    default_type  application/octet-stream;
    access_log    /var/log/nginx/access.log;
    error_log     /var/log/nginx/error.log;

    sendfile on;
    tcp_nopush on;
    tcp_nodelay on;
    keepalive_timeout 65;
    types_hash_max_size 2048;

    server {
        listen 80;
        server_name THE_DESIRED_URL;
        location / {
            proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000;
            proxy_set_header Host $host;
            proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
            proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
            proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
        }

    }
}
```

Then startup nginx with

```bash
sudo service nginx start
```
And check if it is running correctly with

```bash
sudo service nginx status
```

Then, get the SSL certificates with

```bash
sudo certbot --nginx -d THE_DESIRED_URL
```

Replace `nginx.conf` with the new configuration for SSL connections and streaming:

```bash
# Global settings
user nginx;
worker_processes auto;
pid /var/run/nginx.pid;

events {
    worker_connections 1024;
}

http {
    include       /etc/nginx/mime.types;
    default_type  application/octet-stream;
    access_log    /var/log/nginx/access.log;
    error_log     /var/log/nginx/error.log;

    sendfile on;
    tcp_nopush on;
    tcp_nodelay on;
    keepalive_timeout 65;
    types_hash_max_size 2048;

    # SSL settings (updated to use correct paths for certificates)
    server {
        listen 443 ssl http2;
        listen [::]:443 ssl http2;
        server_name THE_DESIRED_URL;
        ssl_certificate /etc/letsencrypt/live/THE_DESIRED_URL/fullchain.pem; # managed by Certbot
        ssl_certificate_key /etc/letsencrypt/live/THE_DESIRED_URL/privkey.pem; # managed by Certbot
        ssl_session_cache shared:SSL:1m;
        ssl_session_timeout 10m;
        ssl_ciphers 'TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256:TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384:ECDHE-ECDSA-AES128-GCM-SHA256:ECDHE-RSA-AES128-GCM-SHA256:ECDHE-ECDSA-AES256-GCM-SHA384';
        ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3;
        ssl_prefer_server_ciphers on;

        # Root directory for the server
        root /usr/share/nginx/html;

        # Load configuration files for the default server block
        include /etc/nginx/default.d/*.conf;

        # Error pages
        error_page 404 /404.html;
        location = /404.html {}

        error_page 500 502 503 504 /50x.html;
        location = /50x.html {}

        # Additional configuration for fastapi (if needed)
        location / {
            proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000;
            proxy_set_header Host $host;
            proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
            proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
            proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
        }
    
    }

    # HTTP server - Redirect to HTTPS
    server {
        listen 80;
        server_name THE_DESIRED_URL;

        # Redirect HTTP to HTTPS
        return 301 https://$host$request_uri;
    }
}
```

Finally, restart Nginx with:

```bash
sudo service nginx restart
```
And check if it is running correctly with

```bash
sudo service nginx status
```
